import BinaryFv.Zesu.ControlFlow.MachineRegions

/-!
# Per-address instruction facts, generated

Generated by `tools/generate_instruction_facts.py` from the machine-regions database,
which decodes the production ELF under pinned LLVM. Do not edit by hand.

`generate_machine_regions.py` computes each instruction's mnemonic, operands and
register write set and drops all of them at the Lean boundary, emitting only
`(address, word)`. Machine-execution proofs then restate those fields by hand once per
site. This table carries them across, scoped to the addresses the proof layer names.

The table is evidence, not an axiom. `instructionFactsMatchImage` checks every row's
word against the file-backed bytes of `Artifacts.programImage` -- the currency
`CodeIntact` preserves -- independently of the Sail-decode check `wordsMatch` already
applies to the same rows. A wrong row fails that check.
-/

namespace BinaryFv.Zesu.MachineRegions

